---
description: Data layer conventions (datasource/repository/Result/State) for AndroidBase
globs: app/src/main/java/com/kira/android_base/app/data/**/*.kt
alwaysApply: false
---

# Data Layer Conventions
- Remote APIs live in `app/data/remote/apis/*Api.kt` and should return:
  - `retrofit2.Response<BaseResponse<T>>`
- Remote datasources live in `app/data/remote/datasource/*RemoteDataSource.kt`
  - They are thin wrappers around the APIs.
- Local datasources live in `app/data/local/datasource/*LocalDataSource.kt`
  - They expose flows (e.g. token/user) and suspend persistence methods.
- Repositories live in `app/data/repositories/*Repository.kt`
  - They orchestrate remote/local for a use-case.
  - They convert Retrofit responses to domain results using `ResponseExtensions.toResult()`.

# Result/State contract
- Network/unknown errors are mapped into `Result.Error` by `ResponseExtensions.toResult()`.
- In ViewModels, map data-layer `Result<T>` to UI `State<T>` via `ResultExtensions.toState()`.

